tests/ -- what runs, and where
==============================

    make test          the shortest check, for anyone: boots a firmware set and
                       requires the banner and OpenBoot's `ok` prompt
                       (tests/smoke/). A few seconds. Needs qemu-system-sparc.
                       On the `sun` path it runs sun-verify instead.
    make test-all      everything below on the gnu path, one PASS / FAIL / SKIP
                       line per gate and a table at the end (tests/run-all;
                       also: make test-full, tests-full). About three minutes
                       with a warm cache. On the `sun` path: sun-verify.
    make sun-verify    on Solaris with the sun path: the sun-built MDs and
                       hypervisor (tests/sun/)

The gates of test-all, each also a make target of its own
(tests/full/<dir>/README):

    smoke   make test          banner and ok prompt
    md      make md-verify     MD well-formedness, reproducibility, pinned
                               hashes (md-verify-reference: vs Sun's binaries)
    boot    make boot-verify   legion booted to OpenBoot: device tree,
                               properties, MD <-> OpenBoot
    hv      make hv-verify     the GNU-built q.bin / reset.bin: GNU as vs Sun
                               as, offsets.h
    workdir make workdir-verify the work directory: made with a marker, cleaning
                               removes nothing that is not ours
    guards  make guards-verify what the Makefile refuses before it builds:
                               MD_MEM, paths, a moved tree, two machines or two
                               makes in one OUTDIR, the wrong toolchain
    tools   make tools-verify  a gate that exits 0 with a FAIL line is a FAIL;
                               the release's md/ bundle keeps every file
    obp     make obp-verify    openboot.bin against Sun's own images
    login   make login-verify  legion booted to Solaris's login prompt; needs
                               a guest disk (GUEST_DISK=<image>), else SKIP
    sun     make sun-verify    the sun path, on Solaris only (tests/sun/README)

tests/run-all runs the gates in that order. PASS: the gate exited 0. FAIL: it
did not (the end of its output is shown, the whole log is kept). SKIP: it
cannot run here (no GUEST_DISK, not on this path), with the reason. Exit code 1
if a gate failed. `tests/run-all -v` shows the output of every gate,
`--only md,boot` / `--skip login` pick gates, `--list` lists them,
`--color never` turns off colour and box lines (they are on only for a
terminal that can show them; NO_COLOR is honoured).

Where the gates work: `make` gives each one a directory inside WORKDIR
(md-test, boot-test, login-test, sun-test, hv-test, obp-test, test-all for the
logs, smoke for the cached firmware set of `make test`). A gate starts with a
clean directory, leaves it for you to look at, and `make clean` removes it
with the rest of WORKDIR. An OUTDIR you give `make` is never used by a gate.
Run by hand (tests/full/md/run, ...) a gate works in a directory under $TMPDIR
and removes it when it passed; with OUTDIR=DIR in the environment it uses DIR
and leaves it.

The gnu path (Linux) runs all gates but sun. On the sun path (TOOLCHAIN=sun,
Solaris) none of the others can run (they need QEMU, python3, sha256sum or the
GNU compiler), so test-all marks them SKIP with the reason and runs only the
sun gate.

    lib/qemu.sh    how the tests find qemu-system-sparc64 (shared by smoke,
                   full/boot and full/login)
    lib/gate.sh    wraps a gate: the gate's own output, then one PASS / FAIL /
                   SKIP line in the format of the table; every make target
                   above runs its gate through it, so `make login-verify`
                   ends the same way as a line of test-all

    config.auto.mk  The gates pin the default firmware, so for a gate target
                   (test, test-all, *-verify, hv-test, obp-test) config.mk
                   ignores what ./configure wrote for TARGET, MD_MEM and
                   HV_UART and exports GATE_HERMETIC=1 to every make the gate
                   starts; the recorded tools are kept. A gate script run
                   directly (tests/full/md/run, ...) is not covered: give it
                   GATE_HERMETIC=1 or a tree without config.auto.mk.
